    "# GestureVision — Assignment 2\n",
    "## Explainable five-class hand-gesture recognition with transfer learning, MediaPipe landmarks, fusion, robustness testing, and a web demo\n",
    "\n",
    "**Course:** Computer Vision, Astana IT University  \n",
    "**Instructor:** Nurym Kaiyrkhan\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook continues the Assignment 1 topic and the same self-collected dataset:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `fist`\n",
    "- `open_palm`\n",
    "- `peace`\n",
    "- `point_up`\n",
    "- `thumbs_up`\n",
    "\n",
    "### Assignment 2 additions\n",
    "\n",
    "1. A1-style **baseline CNN**.\n",
    "2. **MobileNetV2 transfer learning** with frozen-backbone and fine-tuning ablation.\n",
    "3. **MediaPipe Hand Landmarker** as the modern/SOTA component.\n",
    "4. A custom **landmark SVM** trained on the project's five classes instead of relying on an incompatible off-the-shelf gesture head.\n",
    "5. Optional **score-level fusion** of image appearance and hand geometry.\n",
    "6. **Grad-CAM**, 21-point landmark overlays, latency, and environment stress tests.\n",
    "7. Exported models for the Streamlit web application.\n",
    "\n",
    "The system recognizes five static poses. It is **not a sign-language translator**.\n"
   ]
  },
